  "review": {
    "summary": "Reviewer model: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5). This was a read-only static review of the supplied coreReportStateMessage snippet and call-site description only. I found no new BLOCKER, MAJOR, MINOR or NIT defects, and the two UI status-copy findings look closed. (1) Invalid window: 'invalid_window' is handled first, so it returns neutral copy ('所選期間無效，未查詢報表。') whatever `selected` is, and it says nothing about expiry. That matches invalid selectedWindow mapping to false and the request stopping before any DB query. (2) Selected period with no matching report: when selected is true and the state is 'none', the message is period-specific ('所選期間尚無可用報表。'). It no longer falls through to the general video copy or the expired copy. With no selection (null → false), 'none' still gives '目前影片尚無可用報表。'. The ready, queued/running and failed messages switch correctly between the period-specific and general wording. One non-blocking observation, not filed as a defect: the function accepts `state: string` and treats any state it doesn't recognize as '已失效' (expired). If someone adds a new state later, it would quietly show the expired message. Typing `state` as the report-state union with an exhaustive check would prevent this, but nothing in scope shows it happening today. An empty findings list does not certify release readiness: browser checks and remote CI did not run, and I did not run the claimed local results (255/11 tests passing, lint, tsc, PostgreSQL matching) or re-review the SQL matching.",
